# Polarisation transfer in a high-Z foil: longitudinally polarised
# electrons -> circularly polarised bremsstrahlung photons ->
# longitudinally polarised Bethe-Heitler (BH) positrons.
#
# Needs a build with -DSPIN, -DPHOTONS and -DBREMSSTRAHLUNG. Neither
# use_qed nor use_spin_qed is needed: both options are in the
# bremsstrahlung block.
#
# This is the scheme of polarised positron sources (e.g. the PEPPo
# experiment, Abbott et al., PRL 116, 214801 (2016)), here at 1 GeV.
#
# Physics
# -------
# brem_spin_polarisation = T: nuclear bremsstrahlung of electrons is
#   sampled from the screened Olsen-Maximon (1959) cross-section. Each
#   photon gets the mean Stokes vector of its event: a linear part set
#   by the emission geometry and a circular part xi_2 transferred from
#   the electron's helicity. The transfer grows with the photon's share
#   y = k / E of the electron energy, from 0 at y -> 0 to complete at
#   y -> 1. The electron's spin is replaced by its mean spin after the
#   event. Used for electrons with 50 <= gamma <= 1e8 whose final gamma
#   is at least 10; other electrons radiate through EPOCH's original,
#   unpolarised bremsstrahlung.
# bh_spin_transfer = T: the BH pairs get helicities from the photon's
#   polarisation (screened Olsen-Maximon kernel); the photon's circular
#   part xi_2 drives the mean helicities, and the two helicities are
#   correlated even for an unpolarised photon. Applies to photons of at
#   least 20 MeV whose pair leptons both have at least 10 m c^2; other
#   pairs are born unpolarised.
# Both are high-energy, small-angle models of processes in the field of
# the nucleus; see the user manual for their limits.
#
# Set-up
# ------
# A dilute 1 GeV electron beam, fully polarised along its motion (+x,
# helicity +1), crosses a 1 mm (0.3 radiation lengths) neutral gold
# foil. The run stops when the electrons have just left the foil, with
# all photons and pairs still in the box.
#
# Expected (a few seconds on 1 rank; final dump 0001.sdf)
# -------- about 46000 photons and 2400 pairs:
# - Photons ("gamma"): <xi_2> rises with y = k / E_beam and follows the
#   high-energy transfer P_C(y) = y (4 - y) / (4 - 4y + 3y^2) closely:
#   about 0.06 for y < 0.1, 0.5 at y = 0.4, 0.94 at y = 0.8 and 1 as
#   y -> 1. The linear parts average to zero (azimuthal symmetry).
# - BH positrons ("bh_positron"): mean helicity (Spin_*_rf . p_hat)
#   0.05-0.1 overall (Monte Carlo noise; most pairs are soft), near 0
#   below 50 MeV, 0.4 at 200-500 MeV and 0.9
#   above 500 MeV; BH electrons similar. Pairs from photons below
#   20 MeV are unpolarised.
# - Beam electrons ("electron"): mean helicity falls from 1 to about
#   0.92; those that lost most of their energy are depolarised most.
# With brem_spin_polarisation = F the photons are unpolarised, and so
# (up to their helicity correlation) are the pairs.

begin:constant
  # Total electron energy and momentum
  e_beam = 1000 * mev
  p_beam = sqrt(e_beam^2 - (me * c^2)^2) / c
  # Solid gold: 19.3 g/cm^3
  n_gold = 5.9e28
  # Foil position and thickness
  foil_min = 0.25 * milli
  foil_max = 1.25 * milli
  cell = 31.25 * micron
end:constant

begin:control
  nx = 48
  x_min = 0
  x_max = nx * cell
  # The beam (starting in x < 2 cells) has just crossed the foil
  t_end = 4.3 * pico
  stdout_frequency = 10
end:control

begin:boundaries
  bc_x_min = open
  bc_x_max = open
end:boundaries

begin:bremsstrahlung
  use_bremsstrahlung = T
  start_time = 0
  produce_photons = T
  # Photons must move so that they cross the rest of the foil (and can
  # make BH pairs)
  photon_dynamics = T
  # Required by brem_spin_polarisation: electron recoil and scattering,
  # one real photon per emission, no plasma screening (all defaults
  # except use_brem_scatter)
  use_bremsstrahlung_recoil = T
  use_brem_scatter = T
  photon_weight = 1.0
  use_plasma_screening = F
  # Photons below this energy still cause recoil but are not kept
  photon_energy_min = 1.0 * mev

  # Polarised bremsstrahlung: photon Stokes vectors and electron spins
  brem_spin_polarisation = T
  # The lowest photon energy of a polarised event (a physical cut on the
  # events, not the output cut photon_energy_min)
  brem_spin_energy_min = 1.0 * mev

  # Bethe-Heitler pairs, with spins from the photon polarisation
  use_bethe_heitler = T
  bh_spin_transfer = T
end:bremsstrahlung

begin:qed
  # Not needed for these processes; the block only holds two settings
  # that they use (both shown at their defaults):
  use_qed = F
  # collapse: the two BH helicities are drawn as +-1, jointly with their
  # correlation; mean: each lepton keeps its mean helicity
  spin_final_states = collapse
  # F would make every photon unpolarised
  photon_polarisation = T
end:qed

begin:species
  name = gold
  # Neutral gold atoms; brem and BH need the atomic number
  atomic_number = 79
  # 197 u in units of m_e
  mass = 359109
  charge = 0
  immobile = T
  npart_per_cell = 16
  number_density = if((x gt foil_min) and (x lt foil_max), n_gold, 0)
  temperature = 0
end:species

begin:species
  name = electron
  identify:electron
  nparticles = 20000
  # A dilute test beam (no fields of its own) in the first two cells
  number_density = if(x lt 2 * cell, 1.0, 0)
  temperature = 0
  drift_x = p_beam
  # Rest-frame spin along the motion: helicity +1
  spin_x = 1
end:species

begin:species
  name = gamma
  identify:brem_photon
  nparticles = 0
end:species

begin:species
  name = bh_electron
  identify:bh_electron
  nparticles = 0
end:species

begin:species
  name = bh_positron
  identify:bh_positron
  nparticles = 0
end:species

begin:output
  dt_snapshot = t_end
  particles = always
  px = always
  py = always
  pz = always
  particle_weight = always
  # Stored vectors: rest-frame spin for leptons, Stokes vector
  # (xi_1, xi_2, xi_3) for photons (SDF: Spin_x_rf etc.)
  spin_x_rf = always
  spin_y_rf = always
  spin_z_rf = always
end:output
